<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 95,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Thursday 95,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior</p>
<p>Iowa/southern Minnesota hog receipts Thursday were 95,000</p>
<p>head, compared with 100,000 a week ago and 103,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts sold steady with the mid-session Wednesday. Trade slow for light to moderate demand and light offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    56.50 -58.00	   57.50 -59.00</p>
<p>few			56.00 -58.50	   57.00 -59.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    55.50 -58.00	   56.00 -59.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    55.50 -58.00	   56.00 -59.00</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 1.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  45.00 -48.00	   46.00 -49.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   47.00 -49.00	   48.00 -49.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    50.00 -52.00	   50.00 -53.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
